  "all_ingredients_flat": "buckwheat flour, besan (chickpea flour), brown rice flour, whole wheat flour, baking powder, corn starch, kala namak, turmeric powder, onion, green chili, zucchini, sweet potato, carrot, green onions, mushrooms, low sodium soy sauce, water, vinegar, sesame seeds, gochugaru (Korean red chilly powder), spinach, various herbs & spices",
  "instructions": "Mix dry ingredients together. Then add 3/4 cup water. Mix well. Adjust to make dosa batter like consistency. Add wet ingredients (veggies). Spread the batter thinly over a heated cast iron griddle. Cover and cook for a few mins. Remove the lid and cook for two mins, then turn over. Cook until semi-crispy.",
