  "text": "Recipe: Korean Pancake\nCreator: Divya Srikanth\nCategory: Pancake\nIngredients: buckwheat flour, besan (chickpea flour), brown rice flour, whole wheat flour, baking powder, corn starch, kala namak, turmeric powder, onion, green chili, zucchini, sweet potato, carrot, green onions, mushrooms, low sodium soy sauce, water, vinegar, sesame seeds, gochugaru (Korean red chilly powder), spinach, various herbs & spices\nCooking methods: saute\nInstructions: Mix dry ingredients together. Then add 3/4 cup water. Mix well. Adjust to make dosa batter like consistency. Add wet ingredients (veggies). Spread the batter thinly over a heated cast iron griddle. Cover and cook for a few mins. Remove the lid and cook for two mins, then turn over. Cook until semi-crispy.\nNotes: Dipping Sauce recipe included. General recipe components: WHOLE GRAINS (buckwheat flour, brown rice flour or whole wheat flour), BEANS (chickpea flour), LEAFY GREENS (spinach), RAINBOW VEGGIES (zucchini, carrot, onion, green onion), MUSHROOMS (mushrooms), HERBS & SPICES (various). Corn starch: cassava flour preferred. Kala namak: optional. Turmeric powder: to taste. Wet ingredients include 2.5 cups of finely chopped or grated vegetables.",
